  "feedback_interpretation": "Recent measurements support local response modeling and weaken broad corrections. Neutral controls were generally closer than the oxygen-rich, donor-rich, charged phosphorus, acid, and oxidized sulfur regimes. The next batch therefore emphasizes structural controls and condition coverage across aromatic, ester, aldehyde, carbonyl, oxygenated, sulfur-containing, and low-polarity families.",
  "batch_rationale": "The 32 experiments provide broad coverage of neutral hydrocarbons, halogenated aromatics, aldehydes, esters, ketones, oxygen-rich structures, sulfur chemistry, donor-containing structures, and strongly polar heteroatom environments. Ratios span weak through strong eluent conditions, with varied loading amounts and multiple related structural controls. This should improve generalization by repairing extrapolation regions while limiting polar-family corrections from leaking into common neutral rows."
